1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
JSM Portal Answers.
A read-only Forge app for JSM.

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:11,000
A customer asks: what can I request
here, and what must I fill in?

3
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:17,000
The app answers from the portal
itself, through two MCP tools.

4
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:24,000
The real app, deployed on an
Atlassian cloud site, in Jira.

5
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:31,000
Open the Apps menu and choose
JSM Portal Answers.

6
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:38,000
In the Portal field, type SUP.

7
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:45,000
Click Ask about the portal.

8
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:52,000
The answer is read live from
the customer portal.

9
00:00:52,000 --> 00:01:00,000
The portal Support has nine request
types in five categories.

10
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:08,000
Each one: its id, its categories,
and whether you may raise it.

11
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:16,000
The portal rules come with it:
raise on behalf, participants.

12
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:23,000
No invented SLA: what the public
API hides, the app says so.

13
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:29,000
Second question: the form.

14
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:36,000
In Request type, type Get IT help.

15
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:43,000
Click Describe the form of this
request type.

16
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:50,000
The form has three fields.

17
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:58,000
Summary, required. Description.
Attachment, optional.

18
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:05,000
Both answers come from the two
tools of the rovo:mcp module:

19
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:11,000
list_portal_request_types

20
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:17,000
and describe_request_type_form.

21
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:24,000
The page calls the same tools,
so it cannot disagree with them.

22
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:31,000
Every call is a GET: nothing is
written, nothing is stored.

23
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:39,000
Reads use your own permissions,
one scope, no external service.

24
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:46,000
Source, tests and the proof of
the live run are public.

25
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:53,000
JSM Portal Answers.
Answers from the portal itself.
